 ## Overview
-Marching Cubes Vertex List Generation calculates the precise 3D positions of vertices where a scalar field intersects the edges of a voxel grid cell, based on a specified isovalue [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the geometric foundation for polygonal mesh generation by determining *where* the surface cuts through a cube, distinct from the topological decision of *which* triangles to form [30-isosurface-extraction.md]. Unlike [Marching Cubes Surface Point Extraction](6417-marching-cubes-surface-point-extraction.md), which aggregates multiple intersections into a single representative point per voxel for point-based rendering, this method generates a distinct vertex for every intersected edge to preserve topological connectivity for meshing [S1, unofficial].
+This method calculates the precise 3D coordinates of vertices lying on the edges of a voxel cube where the scalar field crosses a specified isolevel, using linear interpolation between corner values [S1, unofficial]. It generates the list of vertices for the polygon(s) inside a voxel based on the cube index, serving as the geometric foundation for subsequent triangle assembly [S1, unofficial]. Unlike its sibling [Marching Cubes Surface Point Extraction](6417-marching-cubes-surface-point-extraction.md), which aggregates intersections into a single representative point per voxel for efficiency, this method preserves topological correctness by generating distinct vertices for each intersected edge, enabling proper polygonal connectivity [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
